   "prompt": "Parallel RLC with $C=0.125\\,\\mu\\mathrm{F}$, $L=8\\,\\mathrm{H}$, $R=20\\,\\mathrm{k\\Omega}$. At $t=0$: $V_0=0$ and $I_0=-12.25\\,\\mathrm{mA}$ (inductor current, pointing down).\n\n```schematic\nC1 0,3 -> 0,0 \"$0.125\\,\\mu\\mathrm{F}$\" i=\"$i_C$\" v=\"$v$\"\nwire 0,3 -> 3,3 -> 6,3\nL1 3,3 -> 3,0 \"$8\\,\\mathrm{H}$\" i=\"$i_L$\"\nR1 6,3 -> 6,0 \"$20\\,\\mathrm{k\\Omega}$\" i=\"$i_R$\"\nwire 6,0 -> 0,0\n```\n\n(a) Find the roots. (b) Find $v$ and $\\dfrac{dv}{dt}$ at $t=0^+$. (c) Find $v(t)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Shape (a).** $\\alpha<\\omega_0$: underdamped.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}\\alpha=\\frac{1}{2(20\\,000)(0.125\\times10^{-6})}=200 \\\\ \\omega_0=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8(0.125\\times10^{-6})}}=1000 \\\\ \\omega_d=\\sqrt{1000^2-200^2}=979.8 \\\\ s_{1,2}=-200\\pm j979.8\\ \\mathrm{rad/s}\\end{gathered}"
