   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "A parallel RLC has $R=5\\,\\mathrm{k\\Omega}$, $L=6.25\\,\\mathrm{H}$, $C=40\\,\\mathrm{nF}$. At $t=0$: $v(0^+)=-10\\,\\mathrm{V}$ and $i_L(0^+)=8\\,\\mathrm{mA}$ (down). Find (a) $i_R(0^+)$, (b) $i_C(0^+)$, (c) $\\dfrac{dv}{dt}(0^+)$, (d) $v(t)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Shape.**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}\\alpha=\\frac{1}{2(5000)(40\\times10^{-9})}=2500 \\\\ \\omega_0=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6.25(40\\times10^{-9})}}=2000 \\\\ s_1=-1000,\\qquad s_2=-4000\\ \\mathrm{rad/s}\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Start (a, b).**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}i_R(0^+)=\\frac{-10}{5000}=-2\\,\\mathrm{mA} \\\\ i_C(0^+)=-8-(-2)=-6\\,\\mathrm{mA}\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Start (c).**",
     "latex": "\\frac{dv}{dt}(0^+)=\\frac{-0.006}{40\\times10^{-9}}=-150\\,000\\ \\mathrm{V/s}"
