   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 3 · ★ AP 8.5: critically damped",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "A parallel RLC with $L=4\\,\\mathrm{H}$ is critically damped with $\\alpha=500\\,\\mathrm{rad/s}$. At $t=0$: $v(0^+)=8\\,\\mathrm{V}$ and $i_L(0^+)=-10\\,\\mathrm{mA}$ (down). Find (a) $C$, (b) $R$, (c) $v(t)$, (d) $i_C(t)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**(a)** Critical means $\\omega_0=\\alpha=500$.",
     "latex": "\\frac{1}{LC}=500^2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad C=\\frac{1}{500^2(4)}=1\\,\\mu\\mathrm{F}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**(b)** From $\\alpha=\\dfrac{1}{2RC}$.",
     "latex": "R=\\frac{1}{2(500)(10^{-6})}=1\\,\\mathrm{k\\Omega}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Start.**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}i_R(0^+)=\\frac{8}{1000}=8\\,\\mathrm{mA},\\qquad i_C(0^+)=-(-10)-8=2\\,\\mathrm{mA} \\\\ \\frac{dv}{dt}(0^+)=\\frac{0.002}{10^{-6}}=2000\\ \\mathrm{V/s}\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Constants.**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}D_2=8 \\\\ D_1=2000+500(8)=6000\\ \\mathrm{V/s}\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Plug in (c).**",
     "latex": "v(t)=6000\\,te^{-500t}+8e^{-500t}\\ \\mathrm{V}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**(d)** $i_C=C\\dfrac{dv}{dt}$ (product rule on the $t\\,e^{-500t}$ term).",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}\\frac{dv}{dt}=(2000-3\\times10^6\\,t)\\,e^{-500t} \\\\ i_C=(2-3000\\,t)\\,e^{-500t}\\ \\mathrm{mA}\\end{gathered}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "(a) $1\\,\\mu\\mathrm{F}$ (b) $1\\,\\mathrm{k\\Omega}$ (c) $v=6000te^{-500t}+8e^{-500t}\\,\\mathrm{V}$ (d) $i_C=(2-3000t)e^{-500t}\\,\\mathrm{mA}$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "fac249fc-9f9d-4aef-9d15-3a9cdec0cb3c",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "936d0835-271a-4e5a-9a77-e86a33553ae6"
