   "id": "e159f0ca-70c7-55b4-abb8-a6902fd9364f"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Goal: a DC current source $I$ is switched in at $t=0$. Find $i_L(t)$.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "5a1bce13-d98f-5cf6-b885-02768ae17015"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Where does $i_L$ end up? After a long time the inductor is a wire, so it carries the **whole** source current:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "ce533392-e99c-58d7-a7b5-2795cb1f35e2"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "i_L(\\infty)=I",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "069d1da4-a13e-53c0-aea3-f117c1c3eca5"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The answer is that final value plus the same three natural shapes as Part B (constants get a prime):",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "79b52429-b7aa-5d1a-b3b6-d70cea7e1c07"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "i_L(t)=I+\\big(\\text{natural shape}\\big)",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "1dda7788-309c-5847-abf9-dcc4c40e8be2"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "overdamped: $\\ i_L=I+A_1^{\\prime}e^{s_1t}+A_2^{\\prime}e^{s_2t}$",
    "critically damped: $\\ i_L=I+D_1^{\\prime}te^{-\\alpha t}+D_2^{\\prime}e^{-\\alpha t}$",
    "underdamped: $\\ i_L=I+B_1^{\\prime}e^{-\\alpha t}\\cos\\omega_dt+B_2^{\\prime}e^{-\\alpha t}\\sin\\omega_dt$"
   ],
   "ordered": false,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "ab85e8cf-d107-5988-9ebc-1ba5109936db"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**The two starting values** come from the inductor this time. The inductor rule $v=L\\dfrac{di_L}{dt}$ gives the slope:",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "a50f0a28-ae3e-59a3-bef0-f3155797d9f9"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "i_L(0^+)=I_0\\qquad\\qquad \\frac{di_L}{dt}(0^+)=\\frac{v(0^+)}{L}=\\frac{V_0}{L}",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "6fb10767-c372-59d3-b68c-92966c0e5fd4"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The constants come out exactly as in Part B, except you subtract $I$ from the start: $D_2^{\\prime}=I_0-I$, $B_1^{\\prime}=I_0-I$, and $A_1^{\\prime}+A_2^{\\prime}=I_0-I$. The slope equations do not change.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "a94da586-803a-547e-ba1c-c863c7543dea"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 5 · ★ Lecture example: one circuit, three resistors",
   "prompt": "No energy is stored at $t=0$, when a $24\\,\\mathrm{mA}$ source is switched in (the switch across it opens).\n\n```schematic\nI1 0,0 -> 0,3 \"$24\\,\\mathrm{mA}$\"\nS1 2,3 -> 2,0 \"$t=0$\" state=closed action=open\nwire 0,3 -> 2,3 -> 4,3 -> 7,3 -> 10,3\nC1 4,3 -> 4,0 \"$25\\,\\mathrm{nF}$\" i=\"$i_C$\" v=\"$v$\"\nL1 7,3 -> 7,0 \"$25\\,\\mathrm{mH}$\" i=\"$i_L$\"\nR1 10,3 -> 10,0 \"$R$\" i=\"$i_R$\"\nwire 10,0 -> 0,0\n```\n\n(a) Find $i_L(0^+)$ and $\\dfrac{di_L}{dt}(0^+)$. (b) Find $i_L(t)$ for $R=400\\,\\Omega$. (c) For $R=625\\,\\Omega$. (d) For $R=500\\,\\Omega$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Start (a).** No stored energy: $I_0=0$ and $V_0=0$.",
     "latex": "i_L(0^+)=0,\\qquad \\frac{di_L}{dt}(0^+)=\\frac{0}{L}=0"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Final.**",
     "latex": "i_L(\\infty)=24\\,\\mathrm{mA}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**$\\omega_0$** (same for all three).",
     "latex": "\\omega_0=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(25\\times10^{-3})(25\\times10^{-9})}}=40\\,000\\ \\mathrm{rad/s}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**(b) $R=400$:** $\\alpha=\\dfrac{1}{2(400)(25\\times10^{-9})}=50\\,000>\\omega_0$. Overdamped.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}s_{1,2}=-50\\,000\\pm30\\,000=-20\\,000,\\ -80\\,000 \\\\ A_1^{\\prime}+A_2^{\\prime}=0-24 \\\\ -20\\,000A_1^{\\prime}-80\\,000A_2^{\\prime}=0 \\\\ A_1^{\\prime}=-32,\\qquad A_2^{\\prime}=8 \\\\ i_L=24-32e^{-20\\,000t}+8e^{-80\\,000t}\\ \\mathrm{mA}\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**(c) $R=625$:** $\\alpha=32\\,000<\\omega_0$. Underdamped.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}\\omega_d=\\sqrt{40\\,000^2-32\\,000^2}=24\\,000 \\\\ B_1^{\\prime}=0-24=-24 \\\\ -32\\,000(-24)+24\\,000B_2^{\\prime}=0\\Rightarrow B_2^{\\prime}=-32 \\\\ i_L=24-24e^{-32\\,000t}\\cos24\\,000t \\\\ \\qquad-32e^{-32\\,000t}\\sin24\\,000t\\ \\mathrm{mA}\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**(d) $R=500$:** $\\alpha=40\\,000=\\omega_0$. Critically damped.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}D_2^{\\prime}=0-24=-24,\\qquad D_1^{\\prime}-40\\,000(-24)=0\\Rightarrow D_1^{\\prime}=-960\\,000 \\\\ i_L=24-960\\,000\\,te^{-40\\,000t}-24e^{-40\\,000t}\\ \\mathrm{mA}\\end{gathered}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "(b) $24-32e^{-20000t}+8e^{-80000t}$ (c) $24-24e^{-32000t}\\cos24000t-32e^{-32000t}\\sin24000t$ (d) $24-960000te^{-40000t}-24e^{-40000t}$, all in mA",
   "citations": [
